this is 38 year old Simon lingard after  he left his home in the UK for the front  line in Ukraine he spent months fighting  Russia's Invasion but on Sunday he  promised his son he'd be home within  weeks he was killed the next day a shot  just thought it was indestructible  with hero to everyone he just stood up  for what he believed in thought to hear  that he weren't here anymore it was just  a really big block at a memorial in his  hometown in Lancashire Simon's family  and friends grieved the loss of a man  who was determined to help others  everyone tried to stop Simon it was his  old man nothing was stopping him if he  wanted to do something  he stood up for what he believed in he  thought it was wrong and he went to help  them  I'm extremely proud of Simon so his  children fly I Soldier Gonna Miss You  Grimmer those who knew Simon Often by  his nickname Grimmy say he had a heart  of gold under a tough shell he struggled  after the end of his career as a  paratrooper in the British army watching  news coverage of the war in Ukraine he  and a friend made up their minds to go  over there we were just like nearly  crying looking at each other and  thinking I've got to do something and he  said I've got to do something Simon  became extremely close to the men he was  fighting alongside he could have left  but he just didn't want to leave him  because they were like Brothers now but  they were like 20 or 30 in them and they  were doing missions and they were  sending them out all over to the front  line and you know the man he's done some  amazing things he's saved many many  lives over there for what he's done the  Ukrainian military are arranging for  Simon's body to be brought back to the  UK his family have already crowdfunded  thousands of pounds to help with funeral  costs to give their hero the send off he  deserves Becky Cottrell Sky News
 

